// REGRESSION: a GUARDED model must transfer a theorem whose proof `specialize`s a LOCAL
// universal step. Before the position-matching fix in `withGuardPremises`, no guarded model in
// the corpus could transfer such a theorem — and nearly every inductive ℤ proof is one.
//
// The shape that broke: the instance's param guards are injected in PARAM order, and the args'
// free variables are APPENDED after the schema's own params, so for a local-head `specialize`
// the antecedent chain is `head -> guard(freevar) -> hyp -> goal` with the guard in position 1.
// Discharging the first (total - prems.len) antecedents as guards then tried to discharge the
// HEAD.
import rational <<< "std/rational.b4m"
import integer <<< "std/integer.b4m"

sort Q = rational.Q
pred isInteger = rational.isInteger

// `integer.negPreimageIsNegation`'s own proof specializes its inductive hypothesis (a local
// forall step) at `succ(x)` under the relativized binder — exactly the broken shape.
theorem negationIsInvolutiveOnTheCut: forall a: Q; isInteger(a) ->
  rational.neg(rational.neg(a)) = a
proof
  @conclusion |
    forall a: Q; isInteger(a) -> rational.neg(rational.neg(a)) = a
    [using model(rational.IntegersInRational) integer.negNeg]
qed
